# SKY-BACKDROP: the procedural sky's parameter block follows the scene every frame (UE: the sky's
# parameters are the view's frame state). Before the fix the block was written from the command replay,
# outside the view's ActiveViewScope, so the sky kept its first block: the sun froze at its load-time
# elevation and a second scene drew the first one's palette.
# 3_colors comes FIRST: opening a scene over unsaved edits stops at the "unsaved changes" popup, so the
# copy (only ZenithColor 1,0,0 differs) is opened right after Starter, before any edit; Starter is then
# reopened for the sun steps, which also proves the block follows a scene switch back.
Дано run Scene "Open Scene Starter.desce"
Когда run Scene "Open Scene SKY_BackdropRedZenith.desce"
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.FOV 60
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,300,0
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.2,0.95,0.2
Тогда-вид 3_colors the zenith is red: the new scene's parameters reached the sky
Когда run Scene "Open Scene Starter.desce"
Когда run Entity "Sun"
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.FOV 60
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,300,0
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.573,0.707,0.409
Когда --subject selection set SunElevation 45
Тогда-вид 1_noon blue sky, the sun disc visible
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.811,0.0,0.579
Когда --subject selection set SunElevation 3
Тогда-вид 2_sunset orange sunset at the horizon, the disc at the horizon
